"""
The Tribonacci sequence is a series of numbers where each number is the sum of the three preceding ones.

Given an array containing the first three numbers of a Tribonacci sequence, and an integer representing the length of the sequence, return an array containing the sequence of the given length.

- Your function should handle sequences of any length greater than or equal to zero.
- If the length is zero, return an empty array.
- Note that the starting numbers are part of the sequence.
"""

# CODE #

def tribonacci_sequence(sequence, length):
    while len(sequence)<length: sequence+=[sum(sequence[-3:])] # While the sequence length is less then the required length, add another calculated value to the end of the tribonacci sequence
    return sequence[:length] # The sequence of the required length
